  "texts": {
    "preamble": "State vs Hitesh on 15 September, 2017 Author: Sandeep Mehta Bench: Sandeep Mehta",
    "facts": "An application for condonation of delay under Section 5 of the Limitation Act has been filed by learned Public Prosecutor in which it is stated that the impugned judgment of acquittal dated 11.7.2012 passed by the learned ACJM, Kherwara was inadvertently challenged by filing an appeal in the Sessions Court which was turned down on 26.3.2016 on the ground of being not maintainable. On these premises, a prayer has been made by the State of Rajasthan for condoning the delay occurred in filing of this leave to appeal application. As per the prosecution case, the Food Inspector, Udaipur conducted an inspection of the shop of the respondent Hitesh on 16.2.2010 and collected a sealed packet of refined Soyabin oil manufactured by G.P.Agro Pvt. Ltd., Kota for analysis. As per the report of Public Analyst, the sample of oil collected from the shop of the respondent did not conform to the requisite standards upon which a complaint came to be lodged against the respondent vendor Hitesh, the manufacturer G.P.Agro Pvt. Ltd. and its representative Virendra Shrivastava. Service of process issued against the manufacturer and its representative could not be effected on which they were declared absconding.",
